# Generated artifacts — a single writer owns the formatting.
#
# Lockfiles are written by pnpm/npm, and the lint-staged globs
# ('*.{json,md,yml,yaml}' and '{apps,packages,functions,scripts,docs}/**/*.json')
# otherwise claim them. pnpm emits single-line `resolution: {integrity: ...}`;
# prettier rewraps it across three lines. The next install rewrites it back, so
# every dependency change produced a ~9,000-line reformat diff on top of the few
# lines that actually changed — unreviewable, and a guaranteed merge conflict
# between parallel sessions. Let pnpm/npm own their own files.
pnpm-lock.yaml
functions/package-lock.json
#
# flash-chamber-cases.json is emitted by
# apps/web/src/lib/thermal/__generators__/flashChamberFixtures.gen.ts and is
# consumed by the external dynamic-simulator work as a numerical gate. Letting
# prettier reformat it desyncs the committed file from its generator, so
# re-running the generator produces a spurious diff and the artifact stops
# being reproducible — which matters because another team gates against it.
docs/thermal/fixtures/flash-chamber-cases.json

